{"animath": "0.1", "canvas": {"height": 540, "width": 960}, "kind": "concept", "level": "jc", "scenes": [{"caption": "Rates that pull each other along", "duration_ms": 9000, "id": "s1", "narration": "In connected rates of change, one quantity drags another with it. As the radius of a circle grows, its area must grow too \u2014 the rate dA/dt is linked to the rate dr/dt.", "steps": [{"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "title", "kind": "text", "size": 38, "text": "Connected rates of change", "x": 120, "y": 120}}, {"at_ms": 800, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The theme: one rate of change drags another along with it.", "id": "sub", "kind": "text", "size": 28, "text": "one rate of change drags another with it", "x": 120, "y": 190}}, {"at_ms": 1600, "do": "show", "shape": {"cx": 300, "cy": 340, "explain": "The pool whose radius is growing: as r grows, the area must grow too.", "fill": "none", "id": "pool", "kind": "circle", "r": 40, "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "strokeWidth": 4}}, {"at_ms": 2000, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The radius arrow: dr/dt is the rate this arrow lengthens.", "id": "rArrow", "kind": "arrow", "stroke": "#1f7a3a", "width": 4, "x1": 300, "x2": 340, "y1": 340, "y2": 340}}, {"at_ms": 2600, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "pool", "to": {"r": 65}}, {"at_ms": 2700, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "rArrow", "to": {"x1": 300, "x2": 365, "y1": 340, "y2": 340}}, {"at_ms": 3800, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "pool", "to": {"r": 90}}, {"at_ms": 3900, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "rArrow", "to": {"x1": 300, "x2": 390, "y1": 340, "y2": 340}}, {"at_ms": 5000, "do": "show", "shape": {"cx": 300, "cy": 340, "endAngle": 60, "explain": "The wedge of new area swept out as the radius grows.", "fill": "#a8d5a2", "id": "sectorFill", "kind": "sector", "r": 90, "startAngle": 0}}, {"at_ms": 5800, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The chain-rule link: the area's growth rate tracks the radius's growth rate.", "id": "chainChip", "kind": "text", "size": 28, "text": "dA/dt grows as dr/dt grows", "x": 120, "y": 466}}, {"at_ms": 6600, "do": "emphasize", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "rArrow"}, {"at_ms": 7400, "do": "caption", "text": "A chain of rates: dA/dt follows dr/dt"}]}, {"caption": "The expanding circle", "duration_ms": 10000, "id": "s2", "narration": "A circle expands: the radius is 2 and grows at half a unit per second. Differentiating area equals pi r squared gives dA/dt equals 2 pi r dr/dt \u2014 substituting gives 2 pi, about 6.28 square units per second.", "steps": [{"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"cx": 700, "cy": 230, "explain": "The expanding ripple: its radius grows at half a unit per second.", "fill": "none", "id": "pool", "kind": "circle", "r": 60, "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "strokeWidth": 4}}, {"at_ms": 600, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The radius arrow: it tracks the growing radius r in dA/dt = 2 pi r dr/dt.", "id": "rArrow", "kind": "arrow", "stroke": "#1f7a3a", "width": 4, "x1": 700, "x2": 760, "y1": 230, "y2": 230}}, {"at_ms": 1400, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The current radius: 2 units at the instant we measure.", "id": "rChip", "kind": "text", "size": 30, "text": "r = 2", "x": 640, "y": 400}}, {"at_ms": 2000, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The given rate: the radius grows half a unit per second.", "id": "drChip", "kind": "text", "size": 30, "text": "dr/dt = 0.5", "x": 740, "y": 400}}, {"at_ms": 2600, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "pool", "to": {"r": 90}}, {"at_ms": 2700, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "rArrow", "to": {"x1": 700, "x2": 790, "y1": 230, "y2": 230}}, {"at_ms": 3800, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "pool", "to": {"r": 120}}, {"at_ms": 3900, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "rArrow", "to": {"x1": 700, "x2": 820, "y1": 230, "y2": 230}}, {"at_ms": 5000, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#1f7a3a", "explain": "The chain-rule formula: differentiate A = pi r squared, then substitute.", "id": "dEq", "kind": "latex", "size": 40, "tex": "\\frac{dA}{dt} = 2\\pi r\\,\\frac{dr}{dt}", "x": 100, "y": 120}}, {"at_ms": 6000, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#1f7a3a", "explain": "Substituting r = 2 and dr/dt = 0.5: the area grows about 6.28 square units per second.", "id": "ansEq", "kind": "latex", "size": 36, "tex": "\\frac{dA}{dt} = 2\\pi(2)(0.5) = 2\\pi \\approx 6.283", "x": 100, "y": 380}}, {"at_ms": 7000, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The units of dA/dt: area per time.", "id": "unit", "kind": "text", "size": 28, "text": "square units per second", "x": 100, "y": 330}}, {"at_ms": 8000, "do": "emphasize", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "ansEq"}, {"at_ms": 8800, "do": "caption", "text": "About 6.28 square units per second"}]}, {"caption": "The sliding ladder", "duration_ms": 10000, "id": "s3", "narration": "A 5-unit ladder slides down a wall, foot 3 units out and top 4 units up. Differentiating x squared plus y squared equals 25, the foot moving out at 1 unit per second means the top drops at 0.75 units per second.", "steps": [{"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The wall the ladder slides down.", "id": "wall", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "width": 4, "x1": 120, "x2": 120, "y1": 120, "y2": 430}}, {"at_ms": 400, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The floor the ladder's foot slides along.", "id": "floor", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "width": 4, "x1": 120, "x2": 580, "y1": 430, "y2": 430}}, {"at_ms": 800, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The 5-unit ladder, sliding as its foot moves out.", "id": "ladder", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#8a5a00", "width": 6, "x1": 300, "x2": 120, "y1": 430, "y2": 190}}, {"at_ms": 1400, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#1f7a3a", "explain": "The fixed relation: Pythagoras ties x and y to the constant length 5.", "id": "pyEq", "kind": "latex", "size": 36, "tex": "x^2 + y^2 = 5^2", "x": 400, "y": 120}}, {"at_ms": 2000, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The snapshot instant: foot 3 out, top 4 up, a 3-4-5 triangle.", "id": "val", "kind": "text", "size": 28, "text": "x = 3, y = 4  (3-4-5 triangle)", "x": 380, "y": 200}}, {"at_ms": 2800, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#1f7a3a", "explain": "Differentiate both sides with respect to time; the constant 25 vanishes.", "id": "diffEq", "kind": "latex", "size": 36, "tex": "2x\\,\\frac{dx}{dt} + 2y\\,\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0", "x": 380, "y": 280}}, {"at_ms": 3600, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The given rate: the foot slides out at 1 unit per second.", "id": "dxChip", "kind": "text", "size": 26, "text": "dx/dt = 1", "x": 250, "y": 478}}, {"at_ms": 4200, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The unknown rate we are solving for.", "id": "dyChip", "kind": "text", "size": 26, "text": "dy/dt = ?", "x": 160, "y": 130}}, {"at_ms": 5000, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 1000, "target": "ladder", "to": {"x1": 330, "x2": 120, "y1": 430, "y2": 216}}, {"at_ms": 5100, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 1000, "target": "dxChip", "to": {"x": 280, "y": 478}}, {"at_ms": 5100, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 1000, "target": "dyChip", "to": {"x": 160, "y": 158}}, {"at_ms": 6400, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 1000, "target": "ladder", "to": {"x1": 360, "x2": 120, "y1": 430, "y2": 250}}, {"at_ms": 6500, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 1000, "target": "dxChip", "to": {"x": 310, "y": 478}}, {"at_ms": 6500, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 1000, "target": "dyChip", "to": {"x": 160, "y": 188}}, {"at_ms": 7600, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#1f7a3a", "explain": "The result: the top drops at 0.75 units per second; the minus means falling.", "id": "dyEq", "kind": "latex", "size": 34, "tex": "\\frac{dx}{dt} = 1 \\Rightarrow \\frac{dy}{dt} = -\\frac{3}{4} = -0.75", "x": 380, "y": 360}}, {"at_ms": 8600, "do": "caption", "text": "The top slides down at 0.75 units per second"}]}, {"caption": "A common mistake: cancelling the d's", "duration_ms": 9000, "id": "s4", "narration": "A common mistake: treating dy/dx as a fraction and cancelling the d's. dy/dx looks like a fraction, so the d symbols look like they can cancel \u2014 but dy/dx is one symbol for a limit, not a fraction: cancelling the d symbols breaks the mathematics.", "steps": [{"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#b00020", "explain": "Scene flag: a classic calculus slip follows.", "id": "mis", "kind": "text", "size": 36, "text": "A common mistake:", "x": 120, "y": 120}}, {"at_ms": 800, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#b00020", "explain": "dy/dx looks like a fraction, so the d symbols look cancellable.", "id": "fracEq", "kind": "latex", "size": 52, "tex": "\\frac{dy}{dx}", "x": 340, "y": 200}}, {"at_ms": 1600, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The wrong move, boxed: cancelling the d symbols.", "fill": "#fde8e8", "h": 80, "id": "wrongChip", "kind": "rect", "stroke": "#b00020", "w": 260, "x": 620, "y": 200}}, {"at_ms": 1700, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#b00020", "explain": "The temptation: treat dy/dx as a fraction and cancel the d's.", "id": "wrongTxt", "kind": "text", "size": 26, "text": "cancel the d's", "x": 660, "y": 245}}, {"at_ms": 2400, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 800, "target": "wrongChip", "to": {"x": 520, "y": 200}}, {"at_ms": 2450, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 800, "target": "wrongTxt", "to": {"x": 560, "y": 245}}, {"at_ms": 3400, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The strike-through rejects the cancellation.", "id": "strike", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#b00020", "width": 5, "x1": 540, "x2": 600, "y1": 240, "y2": 240}}, {"at_ms": 4000, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 700, "target": "strike", "to": {"x1": 530, "x2": 700, "y1": 240, "y2": 240}}, {"at_ms": 4700, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 700, "target": "strike", "to": {"x1": 520, "x2": 780, "y1": 240, "y2": 240}}, {"at_ms": 5400, "do": "hide", "target": "wrongChip"}, {"at_ms": 5400, "do": "hide", "target": "wrongTxt"}, {"at_ms": 5400, "do": "hide", "target": "strike"}, {"at_ms": 5600, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#1f7a3a", "explain": "The correction: dy/dx is one symbol for a limit, not a fraction.", "id": "correct", "kind": "text", "size": 30, "text": "dy/dx is one symbol for a limit", "x": 120, "y": 340}}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#1f7a3a", "explain": "The definition: dy/dx is the limit of delta y over delta x as delta x goes to 0.", "id": "limitEq", "kind": "latex", "size": 36, "tex": "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\lim_{\\delta x \\to 0} \\frac{\\delta y}{\\delta x}", "x": 120, "y": 420}}, {"at_ms": 6600, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "Delta x shrinks toward 0: the shrinking the limit describes.", "id": "dxLab", "kind": "text", "size": 28, "text": "\u0394x \u2192 0", "x": 700, "y": 445}}, {"at_ms": 6900, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The delta-x segment, shrinking toward nothing as the limit is taken.", "id": "dxSeg", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "width": 4, "x1": 640, "x2": 840, "y1": 490, "y2": 490}}, {"at_ms": 7300, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 600, "target": "dxSeg", "to": {"x1": 690, "x2": 790, "y1": 490, "y2": 490}}, {"at_ms": 7900, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 600, "target": "dxSeg", "to": {"x1": 720, "x2": 760, "y1": 490, "y2": 490}}, {"at_ms": 8000, "do": "emphasize", "dur_ms": 800, "target": "fracEq"}, {"at_ms": 8700, "do": "caption", "text": "Treat dy/dx as one symbol: a rate of change"}]}, {"caption": "The connected-rates toolkit", "duration_ms": 9000, "id": "s5", "narration": "The toolkit is always the same: write the relation, differentiate with respect to time, then substitute the known values. The circle grew its area at 2 pi, and the ladder top fell at 0.75 units per second.", "steps": [{"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#1f7a3a", "explain": "Circle recipe: write A = pi r squared, then differentiate with respect to time.", "id": "f1", "kind": "latex", "size": 36, "tex": "A = \\pi r^2 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\frac{dA}{dt} = 2\\pi r\\frac{dr}{dt}", "x": 60, "y": 140}}, {"at_ms": 600, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 800, "target": "f1", "to": {"x": 100, "y": 140}}, {"at_ms": 1400, "do": "show", "shape": {"color": "#1f7a3a", "explain": "Ladder recipe: write the length relation, then differentiate with respect to time.", "id": "f2", "kind": "latex", "size": 36, "tex": "x^2 + y^2 = L^2 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; x\\frac{dx}{dt} + y\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0", "x": 60, "y": 260}}, {"at_ms": 2000, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 800, "target": "f2", "to": {"x": 100, "y": 260}}, {"at_ms": 2600, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The step that always comes second: differentiate the relation with respect to time.", "id": "dChip", "kind": "text", "size": 28, "text": "differentiate w.r.t. time", "x": 540, "y": 355}}, {"at_ms": 3200, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The circle's answer: the area grew at 2 pi, about 6.28 square units per second.", "id": "valCircle", "kind": "text", "size": 28, "text": "circle: 2\u03c0 \u2248 6.28", "x": 100, "y": 440}}, {"at_ms": 3800, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "valCircle", "to": {"x": 100, "y": 215}}, {"at_ms": 4400, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The ladder's answer: the top fell at 0.75 units per second; the minus means falling.", "id": "valLadder", "kind": "text", "size": 28, "text": "ladder: \u22120.75", "x": 100, "y": 500}}, {"at_ms": 5000, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "valLadder", "to": {"x": 100, "y": 335}}, {"at_ms": 5600, "do": "show", "shape": {"cx": 800, "cy": 440, "explain": "The circle, recapped: its area rate came from its radius rate.", "fill": "none", "id": "recapC", "kind": "circle", "r": 20, "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "strokeWidth": 4}}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 900, "target": "recapC", "to": {"r": 45}}, {"at_ms": 6800, "do": "show", "shape": {"explain": "The ladder, recapped: its top rate came from its foot rate.", "id": "recapL", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#8a5a00", "width": 5, "x1": 880, "x2": 860, "y1": 500, "y2": 430}}, {"at_ms": 7200, "do": "move", "dur_ms": 800, "target": "recapL", "to": {"x1": 900, "x2": 860, "y1": 500, "y2": 450}}, {"at_ms": 8000, "do": "caption", "text": "Differentiate the relation, substitute, solve"}]}], "subject": "math", "title": "JC H2 differentiation: connected rates of change", "topic": "h2-differentiation"}